NNAAMMEE
     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg — a script to manage config files for the bluetooth sub
     system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg _s_c_a_n [--dd _d_e_v_i_c_e] [--nn _n_o_d_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg utility is an interactive script to provide a front‐
     end to the complex bluetooth sub system daemons.

     The following options are available:

     --dd       Scan for a specific bluetooth device address.

     --nn       Limit scan to a specific host controller.  Hint: List all net‐
              graph nodes with ‘/usr/sbin/ngctl list’.

     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg will help finding and setting up bluetooth controllers,
     scan for nearby bluetooth devices in pairing mode, lookup their names,
     allow mapping to friendly names in _/_e_t_c_/_b_l_u_e_t_o_o_t_h_/_h_o_s_t_s, ask for the par‐
     ing PIN, instrument hcsecd(8) to securely pair with new devices and, if
     the device offers HID endpoints such as mice or keyboards, configure and
     restart bthidd(8).

     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg can bring up any interface and daemon necessary for op‐
     eration and, if a node is provided on command line, will do so automati‐
     cally for that interface.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/bluetooth/hosts
     sysrc -n bthidd_config
     sysrc -n hcsecd_config

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg scan -n ubt0 -a 00:26:bb:7a:58:95

           This will scan the bluetooth controller ubt0hci for a bluetooth de‐
           vice with the address 00:26:bb:7a:58:95, set up ubt0 if necessary
           and enter an interactive dialog to pair the new device.  Since in
           this example a mouse is paired, bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg will interact with
           bthidd(8), enabling it if necessary and then write an HID descrip‐
           tor to its config.

     bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg scan

           This will scan all bluetooth controllers on the systems for blue‐
           tooth devices, prompting to bring up controllers or daemons along
           the way.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     bthost(1), bthidcontrol(8), bthidd(8), hccontrol(8), hcsecd(8),
     sdpcontrol(8), sysrc(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A bblluueettooootthh--ccoonnffiigg utility first appeared in FreeBSD 12.1.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
